SEQUENCE ALIGNMENT
------------------

Input data: 11 taxa with 4 partitions and 4289 total sites (5.67413% missing data)

  ID	Type	Seq	Site	Unique	Infor	Invar	Const	Name
   1	DNA	11	2730	828	580	1706	1706	COI_pos1+r18S
   2	DNA	10	500	91	22	423	423	COI_pos2
   3	DNA	10	500	363	268	66	66	COI_pos3
   4	DNA	8	559	302	235	218	218	r28S

Column meanings:
  Unique: Number of unique site patterns
  Infor:  Number of parsimony-informative sites
  Invar:  Number of invariant sites
  Const:  Number of constant sites (can be subset of invariant sites)

ModelFinder
-----------

Best-fit model according to BIC: TIM2+F+R3:COI_pos1+r18S,TVM+F+R2:COI_pos2,HKY+F+R2:COI_pos3,TN+F+G4:r28S

List of best-fit models per partition:

  ID  Model                  LogL         AIC      w-AIC        AICc     w-AICc         BIC      w-BIC
   1  TIM2+F+R3        -11802.352   23626.703 + 3.1e-315   23626.801 - 5.35e-317   23691.736 - 7.18e-317
   2  TVM+F+R2          -1192.289    2404.577 + 3.1e-315    2405.027 - 5.35e-317    2446.723 - 7.18e-317
   3  HKY+F+R2          -3566.414    7146.828 + 3.1e-315    7147.055 - 5.35e-317    7176.330 - 7.18e-317
   4  TN+F+G4           -3469.513    6953.027 + 3.1e-315    6953.230 - 5.35e-317    6983.310 - 7.18e-317

AIC, w-AIC   : Akaike information criterion scores and weights.
AICc, w-AICc : Corrected AIC scores and weights.
BIC, w-BIC   : Bayesian information criterion scores and weights.

Plus signs denote the 95% confidence sets.
Minus signs denote significant exclusion.

